  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Ministry of New and Renewable Energy, installed capacity data via the MoSPI eSankhyiki API (mnre/getDataByEnergy). Five energy types (Solar, Wind, Hydro, Bio, Total), monthly from January 2020 to {P.long}, All India and 39 states/UTs. Values are cumulative installed capacity in MW. Retrieved vintage <b id="prov-vintage">–</b>.</p>
        <p><b>Classification break, December 2023.</b> Large hydro (>25 MW) was folded into the renewable-energy total from December 2023. Before that month, the Grand Total excluded large hydro (~47 GW); from December 2023 onward it includes it. The step is a definitional change, not a capacity addition. The guide annotates the seam on every chart that crosses it and never computes growth across it. Individual sources (Solar, Wind, Small Hydro, Bio) are unaffected.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions &amp; uncertainty</h6>
        <p>Capacity is a cumulative stock, revised as installations are registered or retired. The series is final on release. Solar sub-categories (Ground Mounted, Rooftop, Hybrid, Off-Grid) sum exactly to the Solar Total in every month (asserted in validate.mjs). State-level data for small UTs carries interior nulls where no capacity is reported; these are disclosed in the baked file's gaps array.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Energy, version 1.0, covers the renewable capacity buildout: Grand Total (with the Dec 2023 classification break), the four sources, solar sub-categories (ground vs rooftop) and state dispersion. Next scheduled revision: with the next monthly release.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
